in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @fractal
in @fractal/mandelbrot
in @time
in @time/now
in @song
in @song/beat
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/reality/time

# @fractal/crystal — Crystal<T> settled-state species-decl; the
# settled substrate that Mandelbrot<T>.mandelbrot_state.Crystal wraps.
#
# Second species-decl of the @fractal family. Landed 2026-07-20 by
# Mara per Alex Round 2 direct-transcript adjudication.
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# Crystal<T> is the SETTLED-STATE side of the Mandelbrot substrate.
# Per @fractal/mandelbrot: a point INSIDE the Mandelbrot set is a
# Crystal<T> — iteration has stabilized into a bounded region;
# substrate has SETTLED; content is immutable at species altitude.
#
# The three-field shape per Round-2 brief:
#
#   content: T                    — the settled substrate content;
#                                    the T-typed value the Crystal
#                                    holds. Content-addressed;
#                                    identity is byte-equality on
#                                    the T value.
#
#   crystallized_at: BeatOid      — the @song/beat oid at which
#                                    the crystallization fired.
#                                    Composition edge to @song/beat.
#                                    Witnesses WHEN in the saga
#                                    chain the Crystal was formed.
#
#   saga_chain_position: usize    — the ordinal position in the
#                                    @song saga's Crystal chain.
#                                    Zero-indexed; monotonically
#                                    increasing across the saga.
#                                    Witnesses WHERE in the saga's
#                                    Crystal chain the Crystal
#                                    sits.
#
# === Composition with @time/now ===
#
# Crystal<T> is PRODUCED BY @time/now.crystallize. The crystallization
# operation (species-decl at `shards/time/now.mirror`) consumes a
# Liquid<T> at a @song/beat boundary and produces a Crystal<T> whose
# `crystallized_at` is the beat-oid and whose `saga_chain_position`
# is the next ordinal in the saga chain.
#
# Composition edge: for every Crystal<T> c, there exists exactly one
# @time/now event whose crystal_out ref resolves to c. The @time/now
# events form an injection into the Crystal population; each Crystal
# has a unique creation @time/now event.
#
# === Composition with @song/beat ===
#
# BeatOid (the `crystallized_at` field type) is a content-addressed
# reference to a @song/beat (per `shards/song/beat.mirror` `c2bb1d2`
# discipline). Every Crystal<T> carries a beat-witness naming the
# atomic-execution boundary at which it was formed.
#
# The saga chain composition: the @song saga's Crystal chain is the
# ordered sequence of Crystals produced across the saga's beats.
# Position 0 is the initial Crystal (the saga's Crystal seed); each
# subsequent position N is the Crystal produced at the Nth
# crystallization event.
#
# === Composition with @order/fourth ===
#
# @order/fourth (Round-2 species-decl at `shards/order/fourth.mirror`)
# holds the fourth-order metalogue @metalogue(@time/now, @void). The
# observation_fourth carrier's `time_now_witness` field is a REF to
# a @time/now Crystal<T> settlement event — which resolves to a
# Crystal<T> instance per this species-decl.
#
# === SAGA-preservation invariant (Round-2 forward-promised pillar) ===
#
# Per Mara Round-2 brief §Tier 5 forward-promised pillar
# `pillar::crystallization_preserves_saga` (this landed as bilateral
# `crystallization_preserves_saga` at @time/now): every Crystal<T>
# in the saga chain MUST satisfy:
#
#   1. saga_chain_position == prior_position + 1 (no gaps; no
#      re-orderings)
#   2. crystallized_at correctly witnesses the beat-boundary event
#      producing this Crystal
#   3. The Crystal chain is append-only across the saga (existing
#      Crystals are not mutated by new crystallization events)
#
# Compilation-loop-terminates-or-compensates (per Round-2 brief §Tier
# 5 forward-promised pillar `pillar::compilation_loop_terminates_or_
# compensates`) requires that every compilation loop either produces
# a terminating Crystal chain OR issues SAGA compensations that
# reverse the offending crystallization events. Crystal<T> immutability
# is the substrate-decl'd invariant; compensation happens at saga
# altitude, not at Crystal altitude.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/fractal/crystal.mirror`.** Clean mint.
# 2. **@fractal/mandelbrot** (this tick sibling) — parent trait;
#    composition edge declared above.
# 3. **@time/now** (this tick sibling) — producer of Crystal<T>;
#    composition edge declared.
# 4. **@song/beat** (`c2bb1d2` post-Arc-6 extension) — provides the
#    BeatOid type for crystallized_at; composition edge declared.
# 5. **`shards/epistemologic/reality/time.mirror` `snapshot`** — the
#    operational nanosecond-substrate snapshot carrier; Crystal<T>
#    at species-decl altitude is a specialization at fractal
#    altitude carrying additional structural discipline
#    (crystallized_at + saga_chain_position). Sibling altitudes.
#
# === Path-namespace ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/fractal/crystal.
# mirror` declares `@fractal/crystal` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/math/mandelbrot-1980
source @arxiv/practice/void-corpus-2026

prism @fractal/crystal {
  focus  crystal_state
  project crystal_state
  split  crystal_state
  shift  crystal_state
  settle crystal_state
}

# === crystal_state — the settled-substrate carrier (Crystal<T> shape) ===
#
# Typed record carrying the settled-substrate state per Round-2 brief
# three-field shape. Identity contract: byte-equality on the three-
# field tuple.
#
# Note: the `T` type parameter is expressed here as a `ref` since
# mirror's grammar carries type-generic content at ref-altitude with
# content-addressed dispatch. Downstream consumers at rust/fractal/
# altitude (Reed post-Round-2 territory) express T as a Rust generic
# type parameter.
#
#   content              — REF to the T-typed settled content.
#                           Content-addressed. Byte-identity IS the
#                           Crystal's identity.
#
#   crystallized_at      — REF to the @song/beat oid at whose
#                           boundary crystallization fired.
#                           Composition edge to @song/beat.
#
#   saga_chain_position  — the ordinal position in the @song saga's
#                           Crystal chain. Monotonically increasing.
type crystal_state = {
  content:              ref,
  crystallized_at:      ref,
  saga_chain_position:  nat,
}

# === crystal_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, crystal_state) pair discharge admissibility for
# Crystal<T> observation? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.content resolves via content-addressed lookup to a well-
#     formed T-typed value
#   - ctx.crystallized_at resolves to a well-formed @song/beat oid
#   - ctx.saga_chain_position is a well-formed nat (no negative
#     positions)
#   - The @song saga referenced by crystallized_at carries this
#     Crystal at position saga_chain_position (saga-chain consistency
#     check)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; content-addressed
# resolvability; saga-chain byte-consistency check. Sentinel:
# `fractal=crystal-admissible`.
bilateral crystal_admissible {
  sentinel "fractal=crystal-admissible"
  arity 2
}
crystal_admissible(p: peer, ctx: crystal_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === crystal_immutable — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, crystal_state) pair discharge the immutability
# check? Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - ctx.content's content-addressed hash matches the hash the
#     Crystal was originally produced with (no post-crystallization
#     mutation)
#   - ctx.crystallized_at's hash matches (beat-witness stable)
#   - ctx.saga_chain_position matches the saga's chain position for
#     this Crystal (ordinal-position stable)
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; hash equality check.
# Sentinel: `fractal=crystal-immutable`.
#
# LOAD-BEARING: this bilateral IS the immutability invariant at
# species altitude. Crystal<T> is content-addressed and immutable
# by discipline; a Fail here signals substrate-tampering.
bilateral crystal_immutable {
  sentinel "fractal=crystal-immutable"
  arity 2
}
crystal_immutable(p: peer, ctx: crystal_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === read_crystal — the action ===
#
# Given a peer and a crystal_state, discharge the crystal-read
# event: return the content-addressed ref to the settled T-typed
# value.
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the content ref;
# failure carries not-admissible / immutable-violated reasons.
#
# Requires BOTH bilateral predicates to discharge Pass.
#
# Sentinel: `fractal=crystal-read`.
read_crystal(p: peer, ctx: crystal_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires crystal_admissible(p, ctx)
requires crystal_immutable(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === chain_position — the action ===
#
# Given a peer and a crystal_state, discharge the chain-position
# read event: return the saga_chain_position as a substrate-visible
# ordinal.
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the position
# ref; failure carries not-admissible reasons.
#
# Sentinel: `fractal=crystal-chain-position`.
chain_position(p: peer, ctx: crystal_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires crystal_admissible(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === Forward-promised (NOT landed this tick) ===
#
# - Rust materialization at `rust/fractal/src/crystal.rs` (Reed
#   post-Round-2 territory).
# - `pillar::crystallization_preserves_saga` empirical firing at
#   Reed's pillar surface (bilateral landed at @time/now this tick;
#   pillar-surface firing is Reed's territory).
# - `pillar::compilation_loop_terminates_or_compensates` empirical
#   firing — the saga-compensation invariant at compilation-loop
#   altitude. Reed post-Round-2 territory.

out @fractal/crystal
out crystal_state
out crystal_admissible
out crystal_immutable
out read_crystal
out chain_position
